  <p>Formula: <span set:html={rich('[[P=a+b+c]]')} /></p>
  <p>Substitute: <span set:html={rich('[[P=3+4+5]]')} /></p>
  <p>Add: <span set:html={rich('[[P=12]]')} /></p>
  <p>Final answer: <span set:html={rich('[[[\\boxed{P=12\\text{ units}}]]]')} /></p>
  <p>Verify: <span set:html={rich('[[3^2+4^2=5^2]]')} />, which is <span set:html={rich('[[9+16=25]].')} /> The measurements satisfy the Pythagorean theorem, so they form a right triangle: the two smaller squares built on the legs exactly fill the square built on the hypotenuse.</p>

